From bafacaee0cea30f581e0af5c361395fe9434e7a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:34:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Test and document the new solvers of hypre, SuperLU_DIST and
 STRUMPACK

HypreSolversTest (sequential and parallel) and SparseDirectSolversTest
(parallel) solve the Laplace equation with each new entry and check:

- the convergence, the relative tolerance read and set, a null right
  hand side, a resolution stopped by the maximum number of iterations;
- a second operator of the same pattern (the matrix times two, whose
  solution is the half of the first one) for the Krylov solvers with
  the factorized approximate inverse, the hybrid solver, BoomerAMG with
  options (read back from hypre) and the direct solvers reusing their
  analysis; the matrix is copied and scaled, since mfem::Add sorts the
  columns on a GPU, while the diagonal scaling of hypre reads the
  diagonal as the first entry of each row;
- the switch of the hybrid solver to BoomerAMG, each smoother type;
- the options of SuperLU_DIST and STRUMPACK, an operator of another size,
  ParMETIS without the parallel symbolic factorization, the convergence
  report of STRUMPACK;
- the refusals of invalid options.

LaplaceSystem gives the residual of another matrix. The user guide, the
developer guide and the release notes describe the new entries.
